{"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Afluent\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Afluent\/ScI"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubjectSubscription","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"Afluent"}],"title":"SubjectSubscription","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubjectSubscription"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"SubjectSubscription.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Afluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription.swift#L40"},"externalID":"s:7Afluent19SubjectSubscriptionV","symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol"},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/ConcurrentNext"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/AsyncIteratorProtocol-Implementations"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubjectSubscription","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make one with the subject’s "},{"code":"makeSubscription()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". It subscribes when it is made, exactly like the subject’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterator: a "},{"code":"CurrentValueSubject","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s subscription starts with the current value, and every value sent after that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is buffered for it, without limit, until "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()"},{"type":"text","text":" returns it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The difference is cancellation. Cancelling a task waiting in an iterator’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"type":"text","text":" ends that iterator’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subscription and discards its buffer. Cancelling a task waiting in a subscription’s "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()"},{"type":"text","text":" throws"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CancellationError"},{"type":"text","text":" from that call only: the subscription stays subscribed, and a later "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()"},{"type":"text","text":" returns the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values sent before and after the cancellation, in order. That suits a consumer that runs in rounds, such as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch run that is cancelled and started again, and must not miss what was sent between rounds."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The subscription unsubscribes when its last copy is released. It conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncIteratorProtocol","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"operator can read it through ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncIteratorSequence","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"; a cancelled read then ends that operator’s run with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and leaves the subscription for the next run.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Example","anchor":"Example","type":"heading","level":2},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let events = PassthroughSubject<String>()","let subscription = events.makeSubscription()","","let firstRound = Task { try await subscription.next() }","firstRound.cancel() \/\/ Throws CancellationError from that wait; nothing is lost.","_ = await firstRound.result","","events.send(\"launch\")","events.send(\"login\")","let first = try await subscription.next()  \/\/ \"launch\"","let second = try await subscription.next() \/\/ \"login\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wait on a subscription from one task at a time. A call to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" made while another call on the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subscription is waiting throws "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/ConcurrentNext","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and the waiting call carries on as if it hadn’t been made."}]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"A place in a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/CurrentValueSubject","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" that a consumer can stop waiting on and come back","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to, keeping every value sent in between.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/subjectsubscription"]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent"]]},"references":{"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/SubjectSubscription":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubjectSubscription"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/subjectsubscription","title":"SubjectSubscription","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubjectSubscription"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A place in a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/CurrentValueSubject","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that a consumer can stop waiting on and come back"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to, keeping every value sent in between."}]},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/SubjectSubscription/next()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Waits for the next value sent to the subject."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/subjectsubscription\/next()","title":"next()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"next"},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()"},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/PassthroughSubject":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PassthroughSubject","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/passthroughsubject","title":"PassthroughSubject","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PassthroughSubject","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A subject that broadcasts values to multiple consumers without storing a current value.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Unlike ","type":"text"},{"code":"CurrentValueSubject","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"PassthroughSubject","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does not retain the most recent value.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This is an ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that allows multiple tasks to asynchronously consume values and mimics Combine’s PassthroughSubject.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject"},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/SubjectSubscription/ConcurrentNext":{"abstract":[{"text":"The error ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()","type":"reference"},{"text":" throws when another call on the same subscription is already waiting.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ConcurrentNext"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/subjectsubscription\/concurrentnext","title":"SubjectSubscription.ConcurrentNext","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ConcurrentNext"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/ConcurrentNext"},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/SubjectSubscription/AsyncIteratorProtocol-Implementations":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/AsyncIteratorProtocol-Implementations","type":"topic","title":"AsyncIteratorProtocol Implementations","abstract":[],"role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/subjectsubscription\/asynciteratorprotocol-implementations"},"doc://Afluent/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/s16SendableMetatypeP"},"doc://Afluent/s8SendableP":{"title":"Swift.Sendable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/s8SendableP"},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/CurrentValueSubject":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/CurrentValueSubject","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A subject that broadcasts its current value and all subsequent values to multiple consumers."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It can also handle completion events, including normal termination and failure with an error."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncSequence"},{"type":"text","text":" that allows multiple tasks to asynchronously consume values and mimics Combine’s CurrentValueSubject."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CurrentValueSubject","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/currentvaluesubject","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CurrentValueSubject","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"CurrentValueSubject"},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/AsyncIteratorSequence":{"title":"AsyncIteratorSequence","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncIteratorSequence","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncIteratorSequence","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/asynciteratorsequence","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AsyncIteratorSequence","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[],"type":"topic"},"doc://Afluent/ScI":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"_Concurrency.AsyncIteratorProtocol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/ScI"},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/afluent","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"Afluent"}}}